{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794447965,"nonce":"U3zctUYflshhWY2nlBqWPyMSxDg=","message":"Cause found: RenderState::tick calls the scheduler's wall-clock tick(), which steps by the time since the last tick (EMA-smoothed with earlier real frame times), on top of Headless's fixed tick_by. Springs therefore carried real time, and two replays diverged, more under load (the full recorder suite failed on it). AnimationScheduler::set_manual_stepping makes tick() step nothing; Headless sets it. With it, full and patched paints of the no-text scenes are identical (channel difference 0) and the suite is stable. Fixed in a3266638ed96db737880e00e7c3f1445fa233d74 (local, not pushed).","files":null}]}